course: dictionary
lesson: 12534
title: Detach: pulling things apart
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Detach is a useful word with a few meanings, but they all share one idea: separating something from something else. «Please detach the ticket along the dotted line.» You can work out the meaning from the clues: a dotted line is where you tear, so detach means to pull one part away from the rest.
explain: Look at what happens to the thing. «The handle detached from the old mug.» The handle came off by itself. Here, detach means to come off on its own, without anyone pulling it.
explain: Detach can also describe a person. «Mia stayed calm and detached, even when everyone shouted.» Mia did not get swept up in the noise. Detached means calm and not showing strong feelings. The word fits the situation, so you know it is not about a physical part.
explain: Use the swap check. Put a simple word in place of detach, such as separate or pull away, and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have found the meaning.
fact: Detach means to separate one thing from another thing that it is fixed to.
fact: «Detach» is a verb. «Detached» is also an adjective, and «detachment» is a noun.
fact: A detached house stands alone, and a semi-detached house is joined to one other house.
fact: In a story, a detached character seems cold or far away in feeling.
fact: In the army, to detach means to send a small group of soldiers away for a special job.
exercise: «Please detach the ticket along the dotted line.» What does detach mean? | *To pull one part away from the rest | To paint something bright blue | To join two things together | To lose something in the park
exercise: «The wheel detached from the bike and rolled down the hill.» What does detached mean here? | Spun very fast | *Came off by itself | Was painted red | Became much bigger
exercise: «Mia stayed calm and detached, even when everyone else shouted.» What does detached suggest? | Sleepy and hungry | Very angry and loud | *Calm, not showing strong feelings | Lost in a forest
test: «The army detached a small group of soldiers to guard the bridge.» In this sentence, what does detach mean? | *To send away for a special job | To shout a warning | To cook a meal | To grow very tall
test: «The Smiths live in a detached house on the hill.» What does detached house mean? | *A house that stands alone | A house joined to one other house | A house that floats on water | A house made of glass
exam: Which word means to separate a part from the thing it is fixed to? | Attach | Fasten | *Detach | Repair
